Agent B: speed up permission checks.

Adds src/authz/cache.ts, a per-session cache of evaluated collaborator roles
keyed by (session, repository), and uses it in requirePermission. There is no
invalidation: on the base fixture a collaborator's role only ever goes up, and
a cached role that falls short of an action is looked up again.

Derived effect: permission evaluation freshness becomes per-session.

Apply from fixtures/forge-lite on the base fixture: git apply scenarios/s1/b.patch

